<title>SWEDEN: Handelsbanken H1 profit rises 17 pct.</title>
<headline>Handelsbanken H1 profit rises 17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			 3,004  vs   2,572</p>
<p> Net loan losses			    892  vs   1,136</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	    3,956  vs   3,705</p>
<p> Interest income			 19,966  vs  19,503</p>
<p> Leasing costs				607  vs     464</p>
<p> Interest costs			  15,385  vs  14,988</p>
<p> Dividends received			 104  vs	56</p>
<p> Commission income			1,642  vs   1,273</p>
<p> Commission costs			   223  vs     175</p>
<p> Net res of fin transactions	    633  vs     472</p>
<p> Other operating income		   146  vs     321</p>
<p> Total income			     7,490  vs   6,926</p>
<p> Personnel costs			  1,759  vs   1,680</p>
<p> Other costs				1,140  vs   1,017</p>
<p> Total costs				3,534  vs   3,221</p>
<p>Value changes on property</p>
<p>  taken over		     CREDIT    60  vs	 3  CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax charge				   774  vs     770</p>
<p> Net profit				 2,315  vs   1,782</p>
<p> Share (crowns)			    9.70  vs    7.52</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of commercial bank is Svenska Handelsbanken. Anlaysts polled by Reuters expected a profit after credit losses of 3.02 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
